          %title Geometry
          %h2#Geometry Geometry
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            which is modeled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            between them. Here we briefly review the basics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
          %p
            In principle the only
            %strong background
            assumed of the reader here is
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                usual
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} naive set theory
                (e.g.
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets+for+Mathematics"} Lawvere-Rosebrugh 03
            %li
              %p
                the concept of the
                = succeed ":" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum"} continuum
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            %li
              %p
                the concepts of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
                and
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
                of functions on such
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
          %p
            hence essentially the content of multi-variable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+calculus"} differential calculus
          %p We now discuss:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#SmoothFunctions"} Abstract coordinate systems
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#BundlesAndSections"} Fiber bundles
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#SyntheticDifferentialGeometry"} Synthetic differential geometry
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#DifferentialFormsAndCartanCalculus"} Differential forms
          %p
            As we uncover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            further below, we discover ever more general concepts of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"}> space
            ” in differential geometry, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhoods"} infinitesimal neighbourhoods
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie ∞-algebroids
          %p#NotionsOfGeometry
